# Resilient Unstructured Data Extractor

A fault-tolerant invoice extraction pipeline for AD331. The application converts messy PDF/HTML/text into strongly typed Pydantic v2 records, retries failed extractions with targeted validation feedback, and routes irrecoverable payloads to a dead-letter queue (DLQ).

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[PDF / HTML / Text] --> B[Text extraction]
    B --> C[Structured LLM decoding]
    C --> D[Pydantic v2 validation]
    D -->|Pass| E[Validated JSON / UI]
    D -->|Fail| F[Reflection prompt with exact validation error]
    F --> C
    D -->|Retries exhausted| G[Heuristic JSON repair]
    G --> D
    G -->|Still invalid| H[DLQ JSONL + human review]
```

## Key reliability controls

- Pydantic v2 nested models and field bounds
- Cross-field reconciliation for line totals, subtotal, tax, and grand total
- OpenAI Responses API JSON Schema structured output path
- Targeted reflection retries using exact Pydantic validation errors
- Bounded retry count
- Heuristic JSON syntax repair without bypassing schema validation
- Dead-letter queue for irrecoverable payloads
- Streamlit audit UI
- Local demo providers so the reflection and DLQ paths can be demonstrated without spending API credits

